===Etymology 1===
Shortened from {{m|en|woken}} or {{m|en|woken up|woke(n) up}}, or dialectal use of {{m|en||woke|pos=past participle of ''wake'', see Etymology 2 below}}. The sense of being aware of social injustice dates to at least the 1930s.  The derogatory use was most commonly used in the 2020s.

